ly apply to any subsequent Polygon plots unless explicitly overridden.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"iuck6bGxFe"}],"key":"pwiVhlDNiI"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This approach is particularly useful when developing consistent visualizations for reports or presentations. Rather than manually setting dimensions and styling for each plot, you can establish these parameters once at the beginning of your notebook. This not only saves time but also ensures visual consistency throughout your analysis.","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"A7vqnDmyi8"}],"key":"fq2uOFWxnK"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default parameters can be updated at any point in your notebook, giving you the flexibility to modify the styling of subsequent plots while maintaining the efficiency of centralized parameter management.","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"xH0I4bxkWw"}],"key":"c3GbYKUZWG"}],"key":"iGW8LOGKGs"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","data":{"ExecuteTime":{"end_time":"2025-01-08T22:51:50.647943Z","start_time":"2025-01-08T22:51:50.555836Z"}},"children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"hv.extension(\"bokeh\")\nhv.opts.defaults(hv.opts.Polygons(width=600, title=\"My Default Title\", height=300))","key":"l6TiXnc7dp"},{"type":"outputs","id":"cPwTdZH9MYr-qzshRd-YQ","children":[],"key":"iXdcntcTDa"}],"key":"l5q53zsgtG"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","data":{"ExecuteTime":{"end_time":"2025-01-08T22:51:50.753189Z","start_time":"2025-01-08T22:51:50.654728Z"}},"children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"uxds[\"bottomDepth\"].plot()","key":"sfoVSBRyEj"},{"type":"outputs","id":"mwgYgDzTfbu26rwxZpHN5","children":[],"key":"azVEAXxM2O"}],"key":"k1SBbPbsRW"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic Rendering","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"lVV0vEyQ7K"}],"identifier":"dynamic-rendering","label":"Dynamic Rendering","html_id":"dynamic-rendering","implicit":true,"key":"xNu8k0Z77e"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"UXarray leverages hvPlot’s dynamic rasterization feature through the ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"dt0X3i04q3"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dynamic=True","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"c7a4oug72f"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter. This capability automatically adjusts the plot’s resolution based on your current view, ensuring optimal performance without sacrificing data fidelity.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"oNOjb0r5hY"}],"key":"iRHDRwfO8g"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"As you zoom into specific regions of your plot, the visualization engine recalculates and re-rasterizes the data for your current viewport. This means you’ll see increasing levels of detail as you examine smaller areas, revealing fine structures that might not be visible in the full-scale view. This adaptive approach maintains interactive performance while providing high-resolution details where they matter most.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"mIhf7jrfgk"}],"key":"uNHX4hkhgS"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, when examining a global ocean mesh, you might start with a view of the entire grid. Upon zooming into a coastal region, the dynamic rasterization automatically refines the visualization, showing intricate mesh elements and local features that were previously aggregated in the broader view. This functionality is particularly valuable when working with multi-resolution meshes or datasets with varying spatial density.","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"fYF3ZpVj6g"}],"key":"NT4AqUzAh9"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Since the rendered notebooks do not perform the re-rasterization, two GIFs have been provided with commented out code blocks. If you are working on this notebook locally, you can uncomment the code and explore the behavior interactively.","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"Zyg3mNxM1K"}],"key":"iyB5coRPLf"}],"key":"KG9jEjwd8E"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","data":{"ExecuteTime":{"end_time":"2025-01-08T22:51:50.972590Z","start_time":"2025-01-08T22:51:50.792681Z"}},"children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"hv.extension(\"bokeh\")","key":"hHpBXo1cIN"},{"type":"outputs","id":"hX47xwgHFgLGDq5ZyNpwa","children":[],"key":"JDSfF7qa1P"}],"key":"rMpO9gTjHr"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","data":{"ExecuteTime":{"end_time":"2025-01-08T22:51:50.994579Z","start_time":"2025-01-08T22:51:50.992880Z"}},"children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"# uxds['bottomDepth'].plot()","key":"VoiPCJOBRG"},{"type":"outputs","id":"3oY4qIwvaBrfNehmXUpdr","children":[],"key":"IbLssG2c1K"}],"key":"otQFUqcPOi"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/unstructured-grid-viz-cookbook/build/undefined","alt":"bokeh","position":{"start":{"line":2,"column":1},"end":{"line":2,"column":1}},"key":"Kz83slHTM2","urlSo